    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d889">

                <pb facs="0813" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/487.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Clark requests me to say: “Receivers unanimously demand immediate settlement
                    location and deny my right to locate them. Have taken stand on inclosures
                    Department’s No. 27, May 15. Each Receiver seeking to be sustained by his
                    Government. Shall insist on exercise of right to designate location. Vital
                    principle involved. Serious disagreement imminent.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bundy.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
